# Ganesha: The 21 Modaks — Antigravity project rules

- Phaser 3 browser game. NO bundler/build step — Phaser via CDN
  <script>, plain ES modules for src/ files. package.json is metadata
  only, never a required build step to run the game.
- Follow the file structure in memory-bank/projectbrief.md exactly —
  one Scene per file under src/scenes/, shared entities under
  src/objects/, static data (challenges, scoring) under src/data/.
- This is a refactor/polish pass of an already-working prototype, not
  a redesign. Preserve existing mechanics and scoring values unless a
  decision in projectbrief.md explicitly changes them.
- Scoring values are fixed (see projectbrief.md Decision 2). Any combo/
  streak bonus is additive flavor only, capped, and must never push
  the rating bands out of their defined ranges.
- Every mini-game needs a working keyboard control path AND a touch/
  click control path. In ModakRunScene and EcoScene specifically,
  touch handlers must ignore pointerdown events where
  `pointer.y > H - 90` to avoid conflicting with the HUD ability
  buttons (see projectbrief.md Decision 3).
- Deployment is part of Definition of Done, not a follow-up step — a
  phase isn't complete until verified against the LIVE public URL.
- Never mark a phase done without running the game and confirming: no
  console errors, all 5 challenges completable, celebration triggers
  after 21 Modaks.
- Keep asset files optimized (PNG/WebP if any real images are added;
  procedural canvas/Web Audio generation is preferred over binary
  assets where it already covers the need).
- Update memory-bank/progress.md at the end of every session with what
  changed and what's next.
